.TH "OES_TEXTURE_FLOAT" "3JS" "October 30, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
OES_texture_float \- OES_texture_float extension
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]OES_texture_float\f[B]\f[R] extension is part of the
WebGL API and exposes floating\-point pixel types for textures.
.PP
WebGL extensions are available using the
\f[CR]WebGLRenderingContext.getExtension()\f[R] method.
For more information, see Using WebGL extensions.
.RS
.PP
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This extension is only available to WebGL1 contexts.
In WebGL2, floating\-point texture formats and the \f[CR]gl.FLOAT\f[R]
texture data type are available by default (and you must pair it with a
sized internal format such as \f[CR]gl.RGBA32F\f[R]).
.PP
In WebGL 2, you still need extensions to make a floating\-point texture
color\-renderable: use the \f[CR]EXT_color_buffer_float\f[R] extension
for floating\-point color buffers, or
\f[CR]EXT_color_buffer_half_float\f[R] when 16\-bit floating\-point
render targets are supported but 32\-bit floating\-point render targets
are not.
.RE
.SH EXTENDED METHODS
This extension extends \f[CR]WebGLRenderingContext.texImage2D()\f[R] and
\f[CR]WebGLRenderingContext.texSubImage2D()\f[R]:
.IP \(bu 2
The \f[CR]type\f[R] parameter now accepts \f[CR]gl.FLOAT\f[R].
.IP \(bu 2
The \f[CR]pixels\f[R] parameter now accepts a \f[CR]Float32Array\f[R].
.SH LIMITATION: LINEAR FILTERING
Linear filtering on floating\-point textures is not allowed with this
extension.
If you set the magnification or minification filter in the
\f[CR]WebGLRenderingContext.texParameter()\f[R] method to one of
\f[CR]gl.LINEAR\f[R], \f[CR]gl.LINEAR_MIPMAP_NEAREST\f[R],
\f[CR]gl.NEAREST_MIPMAP_LINEAR\f[R], or
\f[CR]gl.LINEAR_MIPMAP_LINEAR\f[R], and use floating\-point textures,
the texture will be marked as incomplete.
.PP
To use linear filtering on floating\-point textures, enable the
\f[CR]OES_texture_float_linear\f[R] extension in addition to this
extension.
.SH FLOATING\-POINT COLOR BUFFERS
In WebGL 1, this extension implicitly enables the
\f[CR]WEBGL_color_buffer_float\f[R] extension (if supported), which
allows rendering to 32\-bit floating\-point color buffers.
.PP
In WebGL 2, use the \f[CR]EXT_color_buffer_float\f[R] extension for
floating\-point color buffers instead.
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] ext = gl.getExtension(\(dqOES_texture_float\(dq);

\f[B]const\f[R] texture = gl.createTexture();
gl.bindTexture(gl.TEXTURE_2D, texture);

gl.texImage2D(gl.TEXTURE_2D, 0, gl.RGBA, gl.RGBA, gl.FLOAT, image);
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]WebGLRenderingContext.getExtension()\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]WebGLRenderingContext.texImage2D()\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]WebGLRenderingContext.texSubImage2D()\f[R]
